  "problem": "If $Y={1,2,{{2}},3,2,4,{{\u2205}},4}$, then $|Y|=$",
  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $Y$ is the number of elements in $Y.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $Y:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,{{2}},\\,3,\\,4,\\,{{\u2205}}\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- Only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\n- ${{2}}$ and ${{\u2205}}$ each count as single elements of $Y.$\n\nSince $Y$ has $6$ elements, the cardinality is $|Y|=6.$",
